": "10-Q", "fiscal_label": "Q3 FY2023", "period_end": "2023-09-30", "section": "mdna", "score": 0.8012, "filing_name": "Exxon Mobil Corporation 10-Q Q3 FY2023", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/34088/000003408823000056/xom-20230930.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "XOM_10K_2022-12-31__risk_factors__0004", "ticker": "XOM", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2022", "period_end": "2022-12-31", "section": "risk_factors", "score": 0.8083, "filing_name": "Exxon Mobil Corporation 10-K FY2022", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/34088/000003408823000020/xom-20221231.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "XOM_10K_2022-12-31__risk_factors__0001", "ticker": "XOM", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2022", "period_end": "2022-12-31", "section": "risk_factors", "score": 0.8033, "filing_name": "Exxon Mobil Corporation 10-K FY2022", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/34088/000003408823000020/xom-20221231.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "XOM_10Q_2022-06-30__mdna__0052", "ticker": "XOM", "form": "10-Q", "fiscal_label": "Q2 FY2022", "period_end": "2022-06-30", "section": "mdna", "score": 0.8563, "filing_name": "Exxon Mobil Corporation 10-Q Q2 FY2022", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/34088/000003408822000051/xom-20220630.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "XOM_10Q_2022-03-31__mdna__0035", "ticker": "XOM", "form": "10-Q", "fiscal_label": "Q1 FY2022", "period_end": "2022-03-31", "section": "mdna", "score": 0.894, "filing_name": "Exxon Mobil Corporation 10-Q Q1 FY2022", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/34088/000003408822000026/xom-20220331.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "XOM_10Q_2022-03-31__mdna__0034", "ticker": "XOM", "form": "10-Q", "fiscal_label": "Q1 FY2022", "period_end": "2022-03-31", "section": "mdna", "score": 0.8387, "filing_name": "Exxon Mobil Corporation 10-Q Q1 FY2022", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/34088/000003408822000026/xom-20220331.htm", "truncated": false}], "collapsed_near_duplicates": 15, "dropped_candidates": 110, "token_estimate": 31930, "gaps": [], "degraded": []}, "answer": {"direct_answer": "In its 10-K for fiscal 2025, ended December 31, 2025, Exxon describes itself as being in fundamentally commodity businesses, so earnings may be significantly affected by changes in oil, gas, and petrochemical prices and refining margins [XOM_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0001]. It says a material price decline could hurt especially Upstream, while a material increase could hurt Energy Products, Chemical Products, and Specialty Products [XOM_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0001]. It also names exposure to changes in interest rates, inflation, currency exchange rates, changes in usage of the U.S. dollar in global trade, and other local or regional market conditions, and notes possible losses from commodity derivatives and other instruments used to hedge price exposures or for commodity and treasury trading activities [XOM_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0006]. The filing points readers to Item 7A for more on market factors; the Item 7A text itself is not in the provided context [XOM_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0006]. The 10-Q for Q3 fiscal 2025, ended September 30, 2025, says market risk information does not differ materially from Item 7A of the 10-K for fiscal 2024, ended December 31, 2024 [XOM_10Q_2025-09-30__mdna__0048]. The language is very similar to the 10-K filings for fiscal 2022, 2023 and 2024, apart from added items such as the U.S. dollar usage factor from fiscal 2023 onward [XOM_10K_2022-12-31__risk_factors__0004][XOM_10K_2023-12-31__risk_factors__0004].", "company_findings": [{"ticker": "XOM", "company": "Exxon Mobil Corporation", "findings": [{"point": "Exxon calls oil, gas, and petrochemicals fundamentally commodity businesses, with earnings significantly affected by price and refining margin changes (10-K, fiscal 2025, ended December 31, 2025).", "citations": ["XOM_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0001"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "It lists exposure to interest rates, inflation, currency exchange rates, changes in usage of the U.S. dollar in global trade, and other local or regional market conditions, plus possible losses from hedging and trading instruments.", "citations": ["XOM_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0006"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Interim 10-Qs say market risk information does not differ materially from Item 7A of the prior 10-K (Q3 fiscal 2025, ended September 30, 2025).", "citations": ["XOM_10Q_2025-09-30__mdna__0048"], "unverified": false}]}], "comparison_table": {"columns": ["Filing", "Market-risk language"], "rows": [["10-K fiscal 2022, ended December 31, 2022", "Interest rates, inflation, currency exchange rates, local or regional conditions [XOM_10K_2022-12-31__risk_factors__0004]"], ["10-K fiscal 2023, ended December 31, 2023", "Adds changes in usage of the U.S. dollar in global trade [XOM_10K_2023-12-31__risk_factors__0004]"], ["10-K fiscal 2024, ended December 31, 2024", "Same factors as fiscal 2023 [XOM_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0004]"], ["10-K fiscal 2025, ended December 31, 2025", "Hedges described as for price exposures or commodity and treasury trading [XOM_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0006]"]]}, "citations": [{"chunk_id": "XOM_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0001", "claim": "Commodity business exposure to price and margin changes", "quote": "The oil, gas, and petrochemical businesses are fundamentally commodity businesses."}, {"chunk_id": "XOM_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0006", "claim": "Interest rate, inflation, currency, hedging exposure", "quote": "changes in interest rates, inflation, currency exchange rates, changes in usage of the U.S. dollar in global trade"}, {"chunk_id": "XOM_10Q_2025-09-30__mdna__0048", "claim": "10-Q market risk unchanged from 10-K Item 7A", "quote": "does not differ materially from that discussed under Item 7A of the registrant's Annual Report on Form 10-K for 2024."}, {"